From: georgii pl <gp@fx.gl>
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: diagnose render encoder aborts on Apple7 (STEAMAC-7Q)

STEAMAC-7Q on M1/macOS 27.2 enters AGX render encoder creation through
cs_start_render. Neither the original event nor its supervisor duplicate
STEAMAC-3 contains an assertion, attachment or descriptor. The existing
Apple9-only diagnostics skip M1. Log bounded render shapes on every GPU
and record Metal allocated/recommended memory for the observed pressure
(22,670 MiB footprint on a 16 GiB host). No rendering behavior changes.

Diagnostic coverage regression: REPRO_DRIVER=kosmickrisp
host/moltenvk/repro/metal-diagnostics.sh <dylib> fails on release 1.9.8
(render=0), passes with this patch plus 0083 on M1 Max/macOS 27.0.1.
This does not claim to reproduce or fix the AGX abort.
---
diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/mtl_encoder.h b/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/mtl_encoder.h
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/mtl_encoder.h
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/mtl_encoder.h
@@ -13,8 +13,8 @@
 
 /* Common encoder utils */
 /* MESA_KK_DEBUG=cbs logs every copy/render descriptor; otherwise each new
- * shape is logged once per thread (at most 256) on Apple9+, or on any GPU with
- * MESA_KK_DEBUG=shapes (M4 encoder crashes, STEAMAC-5E/5F/5H). */
+ * shape is logged once per thread (at most 256): rendering on every GPU,
+ * copies on Apple9+ or with MESA_KK_DEBUG=shapes (STEAMAC-7Q/5E/5F/5H). */
 void mtl_encoder_set_log(bool every_call, bool new_shapes_any_gpu);
 
 void mtl_end_encoding(void *encoder);
diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/mtl_encoder.m b/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/mtl_encoder.m
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/mtl_encoder.m
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/mtl_encoder.m
@@ -165,8 +165,8 @@
 encoder_log_render(id<MTL4CommandBuffer> command, MTL4RenderPassDescriptor *desc,
                    uint32_t *hash)
 {
-   if (!encoder_diagnostics_enabled(command.device))
-      return false;
+   /* STEAMAC-7Q aborts inside AGX render encoder creation on Apple7 too.
+    * Retain the bounded descriptor diagnostics on every supported GPU. */
    MTLRenderPassAttachmentDescriptor *attachments[10];
    struct attachment_shape {
       struct encoder_texture_shape texture, resolve;
@@ -202,6 +202,10 @@
            *hash, encoder_thread_id(), (void *)command, shape.width, shape.height,
            shape.layers, shape.samples, desc.depthAttachment.clearDepth,
            (uint64_t)desc.stencilAttachment.clearStencil);
+   fprintf(stderr, "kk: encoder render memory allocated=%" PRIu64
+           " recommended=%" PRIu64 "\n",
+           (uint64_t)command.device.currentAllocatedSize,
+           (uint64_t)command.device.recommendedMaxWorkingSetSize);
    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 10; ++i) {
       MTLRenderPassAttachmentDescriptor *a = attachments[i];
       if (!a.texture && !a.resolveTexture)
